# K1 / B009 — Run 2 replica annotation (blind).

C R221 OL GOV-010,RUN-015 | MUST | Numeric values in configuration examples are illustrative, not approved defaults; choose retry counts, timeouts and limits from the actual integration and deployment requirements. | Backend configuration | none stated
C R222 OL GOV-010 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | A CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md value must be approved before synchronization; new values are proposed with a reason and approved first. | custom-settings workflow | none stated
C R223 OL GOV-009 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | A conflict between a setting and SPECIFICATION.md stops the workflow until the user decides which source to correct. | custom-settings workflow | none stated
C R224 OL GOV-011,GOV-008 | MUST | Only values that belong in CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md per CLAUDE.md product-source rules are recorded there, not merely framework defaults the project has not intentionally overridden. | custom-settings workflow | none stated
C R225 OL GOV-008 | MUST | Record the setting in CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md with a stable descriptive name, its value and its purpose; avoid duplicating the same literal across many layers when a single source in code or configuration is appropriate. | custom-settings workflow | none stated
C R226 OL GOV-021 | MUST | When a value is added, changed or removed, search for the old value, the setting name, validators/DTO constraints, Domain/Application checks, persistence mapping constraints, frontend validation and UI hints, tests and test data, docs/examples and mirrored configuration; distinguish coincidental numbers and update every affected implementation, validation, configuration, test, documentation and mirrored frontend/backend surface. | custom-settings workflow | Unrelated numeric coincidences are left alone.
C R227 OL PST-009 | MUST | When a setting affects schema constraints, indexes, column lengths or other persistence metadata, update the persistence mapping, create the appropriate migration per the migration workflow, verify Development seeding remains valid, add/update provider-sensitive tests when provider behavior matters, and do not casually alter existing migrations (persistence-change). | Schema-relevant custom settings | none stated
C R228 OL FE-010,GOV-021 | MUST | When both sides expose the same constraint, backend validation stays authoritative; frontend validation and messages are kept synchronized for UX and never relied on for security or data integrity. | Settings mirrored in frontend and backend | none stated
C R229 OL GOV-021,GOV-009,WF-003 | MUST | Before completion search for stale references to the old value, build affected projects, run relevant tests, verify persistence changes when applicable, recheck SPECIFICATION.md for conflicts and run verify; changing one literal alone does not establish synchronization. | custom-settings workflow | none stated
C X36 EX GOV-021,WF-009 | MUST | The custom-settings report lists the setting, old -> new value, every updated surface, any migration created and the verify result. | End of a custom-settings run | none stated | Reporting duty specific to the workflow; WF-009 requires reporting verification state only, not a per-setting surface inventory. | The final message after a settings change must enumerate every updated surface.
C R230 OL DEP-018 | MUST NOT | Containers are optional infrastructure: do not introduce Docker merely because the application can be containerized; build images and deployable artifacts only when the project deploys them. | Delivery and container work | none stated
C R231 OL WF-001,GOV-013 | MUST | Before writing a pipeline or container file inspect the repository (backend, frontend, test projects, Dockerfiles, provider-specific tests, generated clients, deployment artifacts); do not assume a database provider, cache, container or frontend tooling exists, and add stages for the actual project, not generic boilerplate. | delivery-change workflow | none stated
C R232 OL WF-017 | MUST | CI definitions live in source control, reproduce the repository's supported build and test commands, and never hide build or test failures (no suppressed tests, ignored exit codes or continue-on-error for required checks). | CI pipelines | none stated
C R233 OL WF-018 | MUST | Frontend CI uses scripts that actually exist in the workspace's package.json and npm ci when a maintained lockfile supports it; never invent npm scripts and never reflexively replace a lockfile-based install with npm install. | Frontend CI | none stated
C R234 OL WF-007,DEP-003,DEP-004 | MUST | Enforced formatting/analyzer gates only when the project has adopted them; dependency vulnerability inspection per the project's security policy; no automatic package upgrades unless the project adopted automated updates. | CI pipelines | Project-adopted gates or automated updates.
C R235 OL WF-019,PST-004 | MUST NOT | Production database migrations must not run automatically from normal application startup by default: a production migration is an explicit deployment step at a controlled point with the project's approved credentials that fails visibly on error; Development seeding never runs in Production (also unchanged by container deployment). | Deployment / production migrations | none stated
C R236 OL WF-017,WF-009,WF-004 | MUST | Before considering a pipeline complete verify that it restores from a clean environment, builds backend and (when present) frontend, runs the configured tests, does not depend on developer-machine state, does not expose secrets and produces expected artifacts; report each item as PASS / NOT RUN / NOT APPLICABLE. | delivery-change workflow | none stated
C R237 OL GOV-012,GOV-013,ARC-021 | DEFAULT | Prefer explicit DI registration in small and medium applications; add assembly scanning, keyed services, factories or decorators (and Scrutor) only when they solve an actual composition problem — e.g. no Scrutor for a single decoration, scanning only for genuine registration boilerplate and over the assembly that owns the services. | Backend DI | Actual composition problem.
C R238 OL GOV-002 | MUST | Before planning or implementing a new application or substantial feature read SPECIFICATION.md (and CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md when tunable values are involved). | development-workflow | none stated
C R239 OL WF-001 | MUST | Before any non-trivial change inspect the relevant existing code, read the applicable standards for the touched areas, load the relevant knowledge skills, and route specialized work to its workflow (persistence-change, custom-settings, project-structure, delivery-change). | development-workflow | none stated
C R240 OL GOV-018 | MUST | For a questionable request apply the challenge obligation from CLAUDE.md before implementing. | development-workflow planning | none stated
C R241 OL GOV-014 | MUST | Keep the change inside the requested scope. | Implementation | none stated
C R242 OL TST-009 | DEFAULT | For a meaningful bug whose recurrence is plausible add a regression test that fails before the fix and passes after it, unless equivalent coverage already exists or recurrence is unrealistic. | Bug fixes | Equivalent coverage exists.
C R243 OL RUN-012 | MUST | A performance-motivated change identifies the actual bottleneck or cost, preserves observable behavior, uses the simplest effective optimization, adds or maintains tests for affected behavior, and benchmarks or profiles non-obvious or complex optimizations. | Performance changes | none stated
C R244 OL API-022 | MUST | When deprecating an externally consumed API version mark the deprecation in versioning metadata, document the replacement, communicate a realistic migration period and removal timeline, and keep the old version working for the promised support period; never remove it without considering its published support contract. | API deprecation | none stated
C R245 OL GOV-007 | MUST | When a new behavioral rule is approved update the durable source of truth in the same change, including SPECIFICATION.md when appropriate; approved tunable values follow custom-settings and accepted engineering decisions follow architecture-decision. | Approved behavioral rules | none stated
C R246 OL WF-002 | MUST | For substantial feature work or a newly implemented application run code-review (or the code-reviewer agent) before final verification and fix confirmed findings. | development-workflow | none stated
C R247 OL WF-003 | MUST | Before declaring implementation complete run verify at the depth the change's scope and risk require. | development-workflow | none stated
C X37 EX WF-009,GOV-017 | MUST | The development-workflow final report summarizes what changed and why, the verify report, approvals obtained and every unresolved Decision Request. | End of implementation work | none stated | WF-009 requires reporting actual verification state; the duty to report the change rationale, approvals and every unresolved Decision Request is an additional reporting obligation. | Every implementation summary must list unresolved Decision Requests.
C R248 OL WF-006,WF-004 | SHOULD | For container work build the image and verify application startup, required port/configuration, non-root behavior when relevant, health-probe integration and the absence of accidental secrets/files; run meaningful tests outside or as part of the pipeline. | Docker changes | none stated
C R249 OL GOV-013,GOV-012 | MUST NOT | Do not build test infrastructure without a concrete testing need (no enterprise-sized harness for a small project, no generic test-data framework for a few simple objects, no snapshot library by default). | Backend tests | Concrete testing need.
C R250 OL TST-010 | MUST | Convert temporary behavioral checks (ad-hoc HTTP/curl/PowerShell requests, temporary scripts or test methods, manual database checks, regression probes) into maintained tests, verify that an existing test really exercises the behavior instead of adding a duplicate, and review probes before promoting them. | Backend tests | Equivalent existing coverage.

